**Set Application Priority Permanently (Windows 10/11)**

For more performance

Step 1

Go to Task Manager and look for the application or game.
Shortcut key for opening Task Manager: Ctrl+Shift+Esc

Step 2

Right-click the app or game in Task Manager, then select Go to details. After that, again select the application or game,
right-click on it, and go to Set priority.

Step 3

If we set it to Normal and then close the application, when we check again using the same steps (1–2),
it will still be the same — you can see there is no change.

Step 4

On your keyboard, press the Windows key, search for Registry, and open Registry Editor.
You’ll get a popup — click Yes.
Then copy and paste this path:

HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows NT\CurrentVersion\Image File Execution Options

Step 5

Right-click on Image File Execution Options, select New → Key.
We need to rename this key. Before renaming, open the application you want to change.

Then again, right-click the app or game in Task Manager, select Go to details, then right-click it again and choose Properties.
Copy the app or game name from there.

Step 6

Go back to the Registry and rename the key we just created (right-click → Rename or press F2).
Paste the exact name of the app or game that we copied.

Step 7

Right-click on the key, create a new key, and rename it PerfOptions.
After creating it, select PerfOptions.

Step 8

Inside PerfOptions, right-click → New → DWORD (32-bit) Value.
Rename it to CpuPriorityClass.

Now double-click CpuPriorityClass, change the Base to Decimal,
and set your preferred value as shown below:

**🧠 Windows Process Priority Levels**
 
##Priority	     Decimal Value	         Description

Realtime	      256	                  Highest possible risky, can cause system instability.
High	          128	                  Great for gaming, boosts CPU scheduling for the game.
Above Normal	  32768	                Slightly higher than normal.
Normal         32                    Default.
Below Normal	  16384                 Lower than normal.
Low	64	Not recommended for games.##

Click OK, go back, and reopen your application or game.
After that, you can check again (Steps 1–2) the priority will now be changed permanently.

✅ Enjoy — I have tested this and I am currently using it !
